{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kioedi9Q7Qf7vRUeQcbks5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Writer 3 — BestFirst + BreadthFirst + All Bi-directional Finders\n2\t\n3\t## Scope\n4\tBestFirstFinder, BreadthFirstFinder, and all four bi-directional finders (BiAStar, BiBreadthFirst, BiDijkstra, BiBestFirst).\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Priority 1 — src/finders/BiAStarFinder.js (HIGH)\n9\t\n10\t- All constructor options (same gaps as AStarFinder: allowDiagonal, dontCrossCorners, diagonalMovement, weight, heuristic)\n11\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n12\t- `biBacktrace(node, neighbor)` meeting-point path join — start-side expansion finds end-side node\n13\t- `biBacktrace(neighbor, node)` reverse direction join — end-side expansion finds start-side node\n14\t- Both expansion directions meeting explicitly asserted\n15\t\n16\t## Priority 2 — src/finders/BestFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n17\t\n18\t- Custom heuristic injection\n19\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n20\t- Constructor option coverage (same as AStarFinder)\n21\t- The `* 1000000` scaling effect: on open grid, path should be greedy (go straight toward goal)\n22\t\n23\t## Priority 3 — src/finders/BreadthFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n24\t\n25\t- Diagonal movement enabled variants\n26\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n27\t- Start == End\n28\t- Constructor `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` / `diagonalMovement` options\n29\t\n30\t## Priority 4 — src/finders/BiBreadthFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n31\t\n32\t- Diagonal movement variants\n33\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n34\t- `biBacktrace` call from end-side expansion (BiBreadthFirstFinder.js:100)\n35\t- Start == End\n36\t\n37\t## Priority 5 — src/finders/BiDijkstraFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n38\t\n39\t- Same gaps as BiAStarFinder + DijkstraFinder combined\n40\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n41\t- Verify uniform cost behavior\n42\t\n43\t## Priority 6 — src/finders/BiBestFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n44\t\n45\t- Same gaps as BestFirstFinder + bi-directional meeting logic\n46\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d256549e-50d7-46ba-beb2-453bd9daa6a1","uuid":"33d20dd0-0b01-4f3e-a447-9982b90a6201","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:01:33.948Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/test-writer-3/input/assignments.md","content":"# Test Writer 3 — BestFirst + BreadthFirst + All Bi-directional Finders\n\n## Scope\nBestFirstFinder, BreadthFirstFinder, and all four bi-directional finders (BiAStar, BiBreadthFirst, BiDijkstra, BiBestFirst).\n\n---\n\n## Priority 1 — src/finders/BiAStarFinder.js (HIGH)\n\n- All constructor options (same gaps as AStarFinder: allowDiagonal, dontCrossCorners, diagonalMovement, weight, heuristic)\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- `biBacktrace(node, neighbor)` meeting-point path join — start-side expansion finds end-side node\n- `biBacktrace(neighbor, node)` reverse direction join — end-side expansion finds start-side node\n- Both expansion directions meeting explicitly asserted\n\n## Priority 2 — src/finders/BestFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Custom heuristic injection\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Constructor option coverage (same as AStarFinder)\n- The `* 1000000` scaling effect: on open grid, path should be greedy (go straight toward goal)\n\n## Priority 3 — src/finders/BreadthFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Diagonal movement enabled variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Start == End\n- Constructor `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` / `diagonalMovement` options\n\n## Priority 4 — src/finders/BiBreadthFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Diagonal movement variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- `biBacktrace` call from end-side expansion (BiBreadthFirstFinder.js:100)\n- Start == End\n\n## Priority 5 — src/finders/BiDijkstraFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Same gaps as BiAStarFinder + DijkstraFinder combined\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Verify uniform cost behavior\n\n## Priority 6 — src/finders/BiBestFirstFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Same gaps as BestFirstFinder + bi-directional meeting logic\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}}}
